<write simple inequalities to represent a condition>: Writing simple inequalities to represent a condition involves expressing a mathematical relationship where one quantity is greater than, less than, greater than or equal to, or less than or equal to another, using symbols like <, >, ≤, or ≥ to model real-world constraints or limitations.;
<write & analyze relationships between dependent & independent variables>: In statistics and research methodology, dependent and independent variables are the core components of experimental and observational studies; the independent variable is manipulated to observe its effect on the dependent variable, which is measured for change.;
<use coordinates on a graph to create polygons & find side lengths>: Using ordered pairs (x, y) on a coordinate plane to plot vertices, connect them to form polygons, and apply distance formulas to calculate side lengths.;
