<understand base ten place value relationships>: Base ten place value relationships refer to the systematic organization of digits in numbers where each position represents a power of ten, enabling the representation of quantities through positional notation.;
<interpret & compute quotients of unit fractions & whole numbers>: Interpreting and computing quotients of unit fractions and whole numbers involves dividing a unit fraction by a whole number or a whole number by a unit fraction, grounded in conceptual understanding and procedural fluency as outlined in the Common Core State Standards (CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.5.NF.B.7).;
<interpret & compute quotients of whole numbers & unit fractions>: Interpreting and computing quotients of whole numbers and unit fractions involves understanding division as partitioning or grouping, and performing calculations where a whole number or unit fraction is divided by another unit fraction or whole number, consistent with Common Core State Standards (CCSS) for Mathematics (Grade 5, NF.7).;
<solve word problems involving division of fractions & whole numbers>: Solving word problems involving division of fractions and whole numbers entails interpreting real-world scenarios that require dividing a fraction by a whole number or vice versa, using mathematical operations and reasoning to find solutions.;
<divide multi-digit whole numbers>: Divide multi-digit whole numbers is the mathematical operation of determining how many times one multi-digit whole number (the divisor) can be subtracted from another (the dividend), yielding a quotient and possibly a remainder.;
<recognize statistical questions account for variablility>: A statistical question is one that anticipates variability in the data related to the question and accounts for it in the answers; it cannot be answered by a single value but requires data collection and analysis to address uncertainty and variation.;
<interpret methods of sampling>: Sampling methods refer to the techniques used to select a subset of individuals from a population to estimate characteristics of the whole population, as defined by Cochran (1977) in *Sampling Techniques*.;
<understand that probability is between 0-1 & describes the likelihood of an event occurring>: Probability is a measure of the likelihood that an event will occur, expressed as a number between 0 and 1, where 0 indicates impossibility and 1 indicates certainty (as defined by the axioms of probability theory, e.g., Kolmogorov).;
<develop a uniform probabilty model of a single event>: A uniform probability model assigns equal probabilities to all possible outcomes of a single event, assuming each outcome is equally likely, as defined in probability theory (e.g., Ross, 2019, 'A First Course in Probability').;
<develop a probability model of a single event>: A probability model of a single event assigns numerical probabilities to all possible outcomes of that event, satisfying the axioms of probability (non-negativity, normalization, and additivity).;
<understand probability of a compound event>: The probability of a compound event is the likelihood that two or more independent or dependent events occur simultaneously or in sequence, calculated using rules such as addition and multiplication based on event relationships.;
<represent sample spaces for compound events>: A sample space for a compound event is the set of all possible outcomes resulting from the combination of two or more individual events, often represented using organized structures like lists, tables, or tree diagrams.;
<design & use a simulation for compound events>: A simulation of compound events is a modeled representation of multiple interdependent outcomes from two or more random processes, used to estimate probabilities and analyze complex scenarios through repeated trials.;
<solve systems of linear equations algebraically>: Solving systems of linear equations algebraically involves finding values for variables that satisfy all equations in the system simultaneously using methods such as substitution, elimination, or matrix operations.;
<solve systems of linear equations word problems>: Solving systems of linear equations word problems involves translating real-world scenarios into mathematical equations with multiple variables, then finding the values that satisfy all equations simultaneously.;


